ght #D9D9D9 → mid #9A9A9A → dark #5E5E5E with black outlines; tube glass pale cyan #CFE6E8 at 35% opacity with white rim highlight; sample blue #6B83E8 with a lighter top meniscus #93A9F2; field lines and arrowheads purple #8A3FD1; labels black sans-serif with black leader lines. Physics: force on sample F = (χ·A·B²)/(2μ₀); display apparent Δm ∝ χB², beam tilt angle = clamp(k·χ·B², ±9°), tilt DOWN on the tube side for χ>0. Use χ ≈ +1.5×10⁻³ (paramagnetic, e.g. 2 unpaired e⁻) and χ ≈ −2.0×10⁻⁵ (diamagnetic) so the diamagnetic deflection is visibly tiny (exaggerate ×20 for visibility but label it as exaggerated).",
